/**
 * PAYDAY salary corpus.
 *
 * Rules this file is held to:
 *  - Every entry carries a real `source`. Nothing is invented to fill a slot.
 *  - `confidence: 'low'` means the figure is contested, an estimate, or reconstructed
 *    from a contract total rather than a published season salary. Low entries are
 *    listed in NEEDS_VERIFICATION.md (generated by `npm run verify`).
 *  - Soccer wages reported weekly and/or in GBP/EUR are converted to annual USD, with
 *    the original figure and currency kept in `source`. None are rated above 'medium'.
 *  - Pre-1980 figures across all sports are frequently press estimates. They are rated
 *    accordingly and almost never 'high'.
 *  - `leagueAvgThatSeason` is an approximate league-wide mean and is labelled "approx."
 *    wherever it is surfaced in the UI. `null` where no trustworthy figure exists.
 *
 * NFL note: "salary" here means cash earned that season (base salary plus roster/option
 * bonuses actually paid), not cap hit, unless the source says otherwise. Signing bonuses
 * are prorated for cap purposes but paid up front, which is why rookie-deal seasons look
 * so small — that gap is the whole point of several of these entries.
 */

